cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this candidate, its ephemeris or this code, please cite it as below."
title: "TIC 38699429.01: a 2.7 Earth-radius, 11.72-day transiting planet candidate in the habitable zone of the M dwarf TIC 38699429"
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Paliwal
    given-names: Advait
    email: advaitpaliwal@gmail.com
version: "1.0"
date-released: "2026-10-23"
license: CC-BY-4.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/advaitpaliwal/TIC38699429"
url: "https://github.com/advaitpaliwal/TIC38699429"
abstract: >-
  A transit-like signal on TIC 38699429, an M dwarf (Teff 2914 K, 0.166 solar
  radii) at 57.5 pc in the TESS southern continuous viewing zone, found on
  2026-10-20 in a search of 3,883 nearby red dwarfs. TESS-SPOC photometry from
  31 sectors (2018 to 2023) shows 60 transits. Period 11.718167 +/- 0.000013 d,
  mid-transit BJD_TDB 2459196.67148 +/- 0.00072, depth 22,130 +/- 750 ppm,
  duration 1.47 h, radius 2.72 +/- 0.13 Earth radii, insolation 0.66 +/- 0.15
  times Earth's. TRICERATOPS false-positive probability 0.064 with no neighbours
  removed and 0.026 with the pixel-excluded neighbours removed. A planet
  candidate, not a validated or confirmed planet.
keywords:
  - exoplanet
  - transit
  - TESS
  - planet candidate
  - habitable zone
  - M dwarf
  - TIC 38699429
